<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Châlus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Châlus is a small town in the Haute-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienne">Vienne</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of the Limousin, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. While besieging its castle of Châlus-Chabrol, held for the viscount of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limoges">Limoges</a>, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I of England</a> was struck by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crossbow">crossbow</a> bolt on 26 March 1199 and died of the wound on 6 April. The castle keep still stands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chalus.jpg" alt="Châlus" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fonquebure · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chateau_Chalus_Chabrol.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
